# Loads after MenuIcons.lua now (was right after MenuPolish.lua) -- per user report 2026-10-02
# ("this looks horrible and nothing like the mockup"): MenuIcons.lua's generic icon-decoration
# pass runs on every button in Manage Runs regardless of load order, and "Create Run" is one of
# its exact-match icons (an icon + re-centered label), which was clobbering the taller nav card
# layout this file builds for that exact button EVERY time, since MockupLayouts.lua used to load
# (and therefore run its positioning) BEFORE MenuIcons got a turn, not after. Moved here, after
# MenuIcons.lua, so this file's positioning is what actually survives on screen -- it's "the
# approved mockup layout," so it should have final say over anything it explicitly redesigns.
# Deliberately still loads BEFORE BossPacingView.lua (unchanged position) so that file keeps its
# own existing final say over RefreshBossPacingTabContent, which this file also wraps but isn't
# trying to override.
